...

So yeah, every odd term (when n is odd): aₙ = 5,

every even term (n even): aₙ = 3.

Therefore, in first m pairs: each pair (odd and even term) adds to 5 + 3 = 8,

Therefore, in N terms, when N is even like 100,

Number of complete pairs is N / 2 = 50,

Therefore total sum = 50 * 8 = 400.

